# Named owners, per section 1.8 / DR-22 and section 5's layout.
#
# The rule this file exists for: "a floor anybody can lower to make CI green is
# not a floor." Ownership is MECHANISED rather than named in prose, because a
# convention that lives only in a document is a convention nobody is asked
# about at the moment it matters.

# The quality floors (er_f1_floor, er_blocking_recall_floor,
# er_max_cluster_size) and the derived pair budget live here. Lowering any of
# them to make a build pass is exactly the section 21 failure mode.
/dbt_project.yml                    @athvin

# The parity claim and the divergence record. Section 19.4 makes both human
# gates; these entries are what make the human unavoidable.
/docs/PARITY.md                     @athvin
/docs/divergence-log.md             @athvin
/docs/quarantine.md                 @athvin

# The frozen oracle. Section 20.1: a baseline regeneration PR contains ONLY
# baseline changes, and the reviewable artefact is a diff report, not parquet.
/fixtures/                          @athvin

# The gates themselves. A change here changes what every other change is
# checked against.
/scripts/                           @athvin
/macros/quality/                    @athvin
/.github/workflows/                 @athvin
/dbt-bouncer.yml                    @athvin
/.pre-commit-config.yaml            @athvin
